    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (78.43) and **Kyle Schwarber** (71.37) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from a highly favorable matchup against Kyle Freeland. **Trea Turner** is the premier play of the day; his ability to exploit Freeland\u2019s deliberate pace\u2014yielding a 100% success rate on stolen base attempts\u2014combined with a top-of-the-order boost, makes him our catalyst for the scarce SB category. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (71.15) earns a spot as a top-tier start despite hitting eighth; his matchup against Jack Leiter features a high-upside dynamic platoon advantage and a slow delivery, providing the speed floor we demand. **Colt Keith** (67.35) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (64.93) also present strong value, with **Kazuma Okamoto** benefiting from a soft matchup against the 5.14 xERA of Kochanowicz, effectively neutralizing the R/R platoon penalty.\n\nNavigating the bench required difficult decisions, as the optimizer heavily penalized any exposure to elite arms or rain-impacted contests. While **Junior Caminero** and **Caleb Durbin** were high-priority targets, both were scratched due to postponements, leaving them on the bench by necessity rather than choice. **Dillon Dingler** (47.13) was the closest to being squeezed out of the starting nine; while his SP skill matchup is favorable, the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Wacha kept his score suppressed compared to the rest of the infield. We remain vigilant regarding the status of **Christian Yelich**, who remains on the IL, and we continue to monitor the minors for **Zac Veen**, both of whom are unavailable for today\u2019s push. Owners should monitor the wind out at the park where **Chase Meidroth** is playing, as that gust factor is the primary reason his score remains elevated despite a tougher matchup against Luis Castillo.",
